# Performance (Envy)

## Profiling-first
- Don’t optimize blindly: identify the hot path first (CPU, allocations, lock contention).

## Hot-path rules
- Avoid heap allocations and logging inside tight loops.
- Reuse buffers where practical (network read/write buffers, temp arrays).
- Pre-size containers when the size is known (`reserve`, `Preallocate`).

## Avoid copies
- Prefer `const&` parameters for large objects/strings.
- Use moves only when ownership transfer is intended.

## Strings
- Avoid repeated `CString` concatenation in loops; prefer `Format`/preallocation.

## UI responsiveness
- Batch UI updates; don’t repaint/update controls per-item in large loops.
